{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","title":"Local maximum and minimum of a cubic function"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Consider this cubic. Its two turning points are local extrema: one nearby high point and one nearby low point.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"function","region":"A1","latex":"f(x)=x^3-3x"},{"op":"axes","id":"axes","region":"right","x":{"min":-2.2,"max":2.2,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":-4,"max":4,"label":"f(x)"}},{"op":"curve","id":"cubic","axes_id":"axes","expr":"x^3-3*x","domain":[-2.1,2.1]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Differentiate and set the slope to zero. At negative one, the horizontal tangent marks a candidate for a local maximum.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"derivative","anchor":{"el":"function","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(x)=3x^2-3=0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=\\pm1"},{"op":"line","id":"maxtangent","construct":{"kind":"tangent_at","curve":"cubic","x":-1,"length":0.22},"stroke":"dashed"},{"op":"equation","id":"maxvalue","anchor":{"el":"derivative","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f(-1)=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At positive one, the tangent is also horizontal. The curve changes from falling to rising, so this point is a local minimum.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"mintangent","construct":{"kind":"tangent_at","curve":"cubic","x":1,"length":0.22},"stroke":"dashed"},{"op":"equation","id":"minvalue","anchor":{"el":"maxvalue","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f(1)=-2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"At x = -1, does the curve change from rising to falling, or falling to rising?","expected_gist":"Rising to falling, confirming a local maximum."}}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s4"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f748d0cf-c94c-4b1d-833f-c77f226895a3","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The slope changes from positive to negative at the maximum, and negative to positive at the minimum. Local means compared with nearby points.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"maxpoint","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"maxtangent","t":0.5},"label":"(-1, 2)"},{"op":"point","id":"minpoint","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"mintangent","t":0.5},"label":"(1, -2)"},{"op":"equation","id":"classification","anchor":{"el":"minvalue","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=-1:\\quad +\\to-\\quad\\text{local max};\\qquad x=1:\\quad -\\to+\\quad\\text{local min}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
